<title>UK: LASMO eases as Salomon says take profits.</title>
<headline>LASMO eases as Salomon says take profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in LASMO Plc slipped on Monday as the rest of the sector held steady to firmer after Salomon Brothers told its clients to take profits, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1352 GMT, the shares were down 2-1/2p to 267-1/2, trimming the advance sustained during the past two sessions.</p>
<p>Salomon Brothers said it made its recommendation based on share valuations being stretched following recent gains, and said it was targeting the 252p over a twelve month period. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
